{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780839411,"nonce":"vEsY5qYXS0CK68UxhDNc6ap2SLs=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEqDVlA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/229","origin":"github"},"title":"Garmin sidescan: gabby NIC does not link when GCV-10 is connected (mercat does) — 2026-06-05","message":"## Summary\n\nWhile testing the **Garmin GCV-10 sidescan** on **2026-06-05**, **gabby's\nethernet port did not link up** when the Garmin was connected, but **mercat's\ndid**. Testing was moved to mercat as a workaround.\n\n## Evidence\n\nDurable operator note (salmon bag sidecar\n`~/data/logs/operator/2026-06-05/operator_log.jsonl`):\n\n\u003e **13:33:04 EDT** — \"so, gabby's ethernet port did not activate when the garmin\n\u003e was plugged into them, but mercat's did so going try testing via mercat\"\n\n## Why it matters\n\n- The GCV-10 sidescan driver effort targets **gabby** (the Linux/ROS host) for\n  the eventual on-boat ROS driver. If gabby's NIC won't link to the Garmin, the\n  on-boat integration path is blocked.\n- mercat linking but gabby not points to a **gabby-side** NIC config /\n  link-negotiation / cabling issue rather than a Garmin fault.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- Check gabby NIC on Garmin connect: link auto-negotiation (speed/duplex/\n  auto-MDIX), whether the interface is admin-up, `dmesg` / `ip link` on plug-in,\n  and cabling (the GCV-10 may expect a specific link config).\n- Diff gabby's NIC settings against mercat's working port.\n- Part of the parallel Garmin sidescan driver effort.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}